# PhoneLab environment
#
# Copy to .env.local and adjust. Every value below is optional: with no .env at all,
# PhoneLab runs on the file-backed local storage driver, which is the intended
# experience for `npm run dev`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment identity
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public origin of this deployment, with no trailing slash.
#
# Set this in production. It is the base for the MCP connector URL, the OAuth
# issuer, and the resource identifier that access tokens are bound to (RFC 8707) —
# so if it is wrong, Claude's tokens will be rejected. Left unset, PhoneLab derives
# it from the request's forwarded host, which is fine locally.
# PHONELAB_BASE_URL=https://phonelab.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `local`    — JSON file under PHONELAB_DATA_DIR. Default. Single node only.
# `supabase` — Postgres. Requires the two variables below.
#
# Omit this and PhoneLab picks Supabase automatically when both Supabase variables
# are present, otherwise the local driver.
# PHONELAB_STORE=local

# Where the local driver keeps its data. Defaults to ./.phonelab-data
# PHONELAB_DATA_DIR=./.phonelab-data

# Postgres via Supabase. The service-role key must never reach the browser: it is
# only read by server code, behind PhoneLab's own authorisation checks.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here, and there should not be. PhoneLab does not
# call a model API: users connect it to Claude as a custom connector and use their
# own subscription. PhoneLab provides the tools; Claude decides when to call them.
